/P 63 0 R
/E (The Stock Price Analyzer follows a modular approach. The user enters stock information through the graphical user interface. The input is validated and passed to the StockManager class, which stores the records in an ArrayList. A Stack is used to support the undo operation, while a Queue maintains the five most recently added stock records.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 63 0 R
/E (The StockAlgorithms class performs searching, sorting and statistical operations. Merge Sort is used to sort stock prices, Linear Search is used to find company records and Binary Search is used to locate stock prices in sorted data. The StockChartPanel class displays the stock price trend graphically. The records are saved to a file using serialization.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
