564 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Stock Price Analyzer is a Java-based application developed to manage and analyze manually entered stock price records. The application provides a graphical user interface through which users can enter company names, dates and stock prices, store records, search and sort data, and analyze stock price trends. It uses data structures such as ArrayList, Stack and Queue, along with algorithms including Linear Search, Binary Search and Merge Sort. The system also provides statistical calculations such as maximum, minimum and average stock price and displays stock price trends through graphical charts. The records are stored using file handling and serialization, allowing data to be retained even after the application is closed. The project demonstrates the practical implementation of Data Structures and Algorithms using Java.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 501 0 R
>>
endobj
